  "notes": {
    "fgn-dark-odyssey": "My FGN six-string with Fishman Fluence Modern pickups installed. I call it the Dark Odyssey; the exact model code is still to be checked. The pickups are part of this guitar.",
    "fender-duo-sonic": "My gold-colored Fender Duo-Sonic. I think the finish is Desert Sand; the finish and year are unconfirmed. The catalog link covers the model family.",
    "tuner-unconfirmed": "My tuner, connected to the G3S AUX output rather than inserted among the effect loops.",
    "boss-ns2": "Listens to the clean guitar, then closes after the drives and compressor. Reverb stays outside the gate.",
    "kaede": "An alternate overdrive voice, with bass, treble and selectable headroom. A choice alongside Galea and Lightspeed.",
    "knife-drop": "Octave, fuzz and synth textures. The space preset leaves the gate out so slower envelopes can breathe.",
    "greer-lightspeed": "My low-gain voice for edge and touch-sensitive rhythm sounds.",
    "friedman-beod": "The high-gain voice. I prefer the compressor after it to even the level and extend sustain.",
    "keeley-compressor-plus": "After the drives, where I like it. Blends compression with the dry signal to control level and sustain.",
    "keeley-dyno-my-roto": "Chorus, rotary and flange movement, after the gate.",
    "swan-hunter": "Lo-fi echo and reverb for the moments that need space. A situational texture rather than an always-on delay.",
    "harmonic-tremolo-unconfirmed": "Rhythmic movement after the gate. A separate texture to call up when the part needs a pulse.",
    "boss-rc1": "Owned and kept off this board plan. Still available for straightforward looping in another setup.",
    "op1-field": "External recorder and instrument. Receives OPUS headphone audio; headphones move to the OP-1 while recording.",
    "orange-crush-20rt": "My real amp, fed at the front input from the isolated G3S output. This model has no effects loop.",
    "empress-paraeq": "Planned final tone shaping in loop 12, after modulation and space.",
    "vemuram-galea": "Planned overdrive voice for the Galea presets. Purchase completion is still to be confirmed.",
    "two-notes-opus": "The planned amp and cabinet voice for direct recording and headphones. USB handles editing; audio leaves through its analog outputs.",
    "gigrig-g3s": "Recalls selected loops and their order. Presets do not move the pedals’ physical knobs.",
    "gigrig-genx14": "Planned isolated power distribution. Its supplied 24 V adapter feeds the system; pedals use rated DC outputs.",
    "gigrig-genx4lc": "Four-output power expansion for the GENX14 system. It does not add audio loops to the G3S.",
    "schmidt-sa550xdm": "Ordered from Schmidt Array. The two-floor layout is planned; final plug clearance is checked by the builder.",
    "lehle-dual-expression": "Planned expression control through G3S. It can send an assigned MIDI value without carrying guitar audio.",
    "cme-h4midi-wc": "Routes G3S commands to OPUS and the external MIDI port. The proposed power combiner still needs builder approval.",
    "cme-c2midi-pro": "Planned DIN-to-USB MIDI interface. OP-1 field hosts it for standalone foot control.",
    "canvas-power-6": "My existing Walrus Canvas supply, kept off the main board. I have called it Power 6; the exact model needs checking before adding a catalog link.",
    "genx14-adapter": "Included with GENX14. The lower deck reserves space for the adapter; this is not a separate pedal purchase.",
    "schmidt-connector-box": "Board-edge access for guitar, amp and the OPUS headphone feed. Installation details remain part of the build order.",
    "schmidt-rear-patchbay": "Rear connections for OPUS line out and auxiliary input, with two spare channels.",
    "schmidt-socket-plate": "Planned XLR, MIDI and two separate USB data connections. Final hardware configuration needs supplier confirmation.",
    "photo-accessories-unconfirmed": "A treadle pedal and two small dial controllers appear in the collection photo. Their exact models and current use need confirmation.",
    "te-ep35": "A portable speaker option for the OP-1 field output. Purchase is unconfirmed. Feed its stereo line input; the board still needs its own power.",
    "te-ep127": "Owned foot controller for the EP-35. It can pair wirelessly for amp controls. It stays outside the G3S audio loops; it is a controller, not an audio effect in the guitar chain."
  },
